# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the fusion programme's WP1 jobs (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of the fusion integration branch and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a
# registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from here. ONE IMAGE FOR THE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-fusion-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for the
# tag the integrator's build job produces from the integration commit (sed -i 's/tp4-fusion-1/<tag>/' *.env); a commit of a file the image carries needs a new build and tag.
# These jobs add to the generated pack in scripts/ci/references/fusion-jobs (make_fusion_jobs.py: <ID>A audited attach and the timed ABAB of the one-core fold, lever id s1): the card-M job
# C1 that runs FIRST, the tree-fold variants (lever twins s1f2) and the trace_ms read of the ABAB.
# T2: ARM B (the lever) of the ABAB (A control, B lever, A control, B lever) on trace_ms, audits OFF. B = c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-s1f2, the control plus exactly QWEN_FAST_TP4_SHARD_ARGMAX=1 and QWEN_FAST_TP4_SHARD_ARGMAX_FOLD2=1 (the tree fold). Arms alternate in this one image, each after its own all-four reset, same admission order.
# Tests: warmup, coding, concurrent8_steady, concurrent8_code_32k, concurrent8_code_128k (the earlier S1 pair's mix: 4k, 32k and 128k contexts, 8 users, 800 tokens out).
# READ with optimisation/ttnn-op/shard_argmax/trace_ms_abab.py --control <T1 container.log> <T3 container.log> --lever <T2 container.log> <T4 container.log> (T2alt/T4alt for the one-core fold): the median [PACKED-PHASE]
# trace_ms of the 64-row block verifies (live=4), per pair and per third of the run, with the host phases beside it. NEVER judge S1 by the aggregate tok/s of a smoke test: it carries the host (TS2, the only earlier
# S1 timing, read 135 tok/s at 32k against controls of 156 and 158 while its trace_ms was 0.70 ms LOWER; its input_ms was 2.3 ms higher: host contention; the repeat read parity). Pass: PASS from the script (every pair saves at
# least 0.5 ms of trace_ms in every third; 0.74 ms is what the one-core fold measured, the tree is estimated at 0.85 to 0.95), the texts equal to the control's (speed_window_compare exit 0), and no 'fell back' line
# (tp4_shard_argmax_smoke.problems). The generated pack's w2ln_timing_compare pair read (<ID>C1 L1 C2 L2) is the round-level companion. Check the load average around the run (a busy host skews host phases 10 to 20 percent)
# and keep the rig's CI runner sets scaled down for the block. Duration (estimate): 50 min.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-fusion-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-s1f2
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,concurrent8_steady,concurrent8_code_32k,concurrent8_code_128k
